{"archetypes":[{"name":"glob-safety","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan adds multiple glob patterns to a denylist; verify each pattern is neither over-broad (matches canonical artifacts) nor under-broad (misses real producer variants like phased outputs).","prompt_body":"Examine every new glob pattern added to design_artifact_excluded() in scripts/design-log-publish.sh — specifically cursor-plan-*-output*.txt, codex-primary-plan-*-output*.txt, claude-plan-*-output*.txt, and each sidecar suffix arm. For each pattern, verify it cannot match canonical published artifacts like findings.md, voting-tally.md, or voter-output-*.json. Confirm that the *-output*.txt wildcard correctly covers phased waterfall names (e.g., -output-phase2.txt, -output-phase3.txt) without inadvertently matching other output files that should be published. Check whether the sidecar suffix exclusions (e.g., .meta, .cap-hit, .tsv) could match non-plan-review files that share those suffixes and would be incorrectly excluded. Identify any glob that is either too aggressive or too narrow relative to the plan's stated intent of excluding only raw reviewer transcripts and diagnostics. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"fixture-parity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan adds many new test fixtures; verify each new deny arm in design_artifact_excluded() has a matching assert_excluded fixture and no canonical artifact loses its assert_included counterpart.","prompt_body":"Cross-check every new exclusion arm added to design_artifact_excluded() in scripts/design-log-publish.sh against the fixture list planned for scripts/test-design-log-publish.sh. Each arm (transcript family, sidecar suffix, collector failure log, dropped-slot diagnostic, generic prompt) must have at least one explicit assert_excluded fixture; identify any arm that lacks a corresponding fixture. Conversely, verify that canonical artifacts preserved by the plan — findings.md, voting-tally.md, voter-output-*.json, and any existing assert_included items — still appear in positive assertions and would not be accidentally caught by the new patterns. Check whether the plan's listed fixtures (e.g., claude-plan-generic-output.txt, plan-review-slots.ndjson.output-files.dropped-slots) are actually wired into the deny-list assertion loop and not merely created as files without assertions. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"producer-name-audit","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The fix exists to align patterns with real producer file names; verify each exclusion pattern matches actual emitted names from dispatch-plan-review-panel.sh and related scripts with no dead patterns reintroduced.","prompt_body":"Audit each exclusion pattern in the plan against what real producer scripts actually emit by locating dispatch-plan-review-panel.sh and any other scripts that write plan-review output files and extracting their actual file-name templates. Verify that cursor-plan-*-output*.txt, codex-primary-plan-*-output*.txt, and claude-plan-*-output*.txt each match real produced names and that no pattern reverts to the dead codex-plan-* form the issue specifically identified as incorrect. Check whether collector failure log names used in the plan's test fixtures (e.g., cursor-plan-*-collector.failure.log) match the naming convention used by the actual collector scripts. Flag any pattern in the plan that targets a file name not confirmed in any producer script, and any real producer output that falls outside all deny patterns. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
